#: src/communication.md:1
msgid "Communication"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:3
msgid ""
"This page explains how a program communicates with the system components."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:5
msgid "TODO: verify if outdated information is present"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:9
msgid "A scheme is a system service"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:10
msgid "SQE means \"Submission Queue Entry\""
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:11
msgid "CQE means \"Completion Queue Entry\""
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:12
msgid ""
"POSIX and Linux functions are implemented by relibc using Redox services "
"provided by schemes, they work with the Applicationropriate schemes to "
"implement the function. It might involve opening a scheme, maybe writing to "
"a scheme, or maybe calling `mmap` on the scheme after opening (this is "
"pretty common)."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:13
msgid ""
"relibc and redox-rt talk to the scheme via a system call - open, read, "
"write, mmap, etc."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:14
msgid ""
"A system component (userspace daemon) uses the Scheme API (from the `redox-"
"scheme` library) to implement the system service. The Scheme API also is "
"doing system calls like `open`, `read` and `write`, but the message format "
"for reading and writing is a special format. The latest version of the "
"Scheme API reads SQE messages and writes CQE messages. SQE is basically the "
"parameters to the system call that the caller originally did, packaged into "
"a message. CQE is the response that the daemon sends back."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:15
msgid ""
"The kernel is responsible for creating the SQE messages, and for unpacking "
"the CQE messages."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:17
msgid "System Function Usage Example"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:19
msgid ""
"The following sequence explain how a application using a system function "
"happens in Redox communication design."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:21
msgid "The program calls some POSIX or Linux function from relibc"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:22
msgid "relibc/redox-rt convert it to system calls"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:23
msgid "The kernel converts the system calls to SQE"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:24
msgid ""
"The userspace daemon calls read on a \"scheme socket\" and gets an SQE "
"message"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:25
msgid ""
"The userspace daemon calls write on the scheme socket and sends a CQE message"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:26
msgid "The kernel converts the CQE message to the result of the system call"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:27
msgid ""
"relibc/redox-rt gets the result from the system call and uses that to "
"calculate the result of the POSIX or Linux function call"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:29
msgid "File Access Design Example"
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:31
msgid ""
"The following event sequence explain how a file access using namespaces and "
"capabilities happens in Redox communication design."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:33
msgid ""
"Application -> Kernel: The application calls the `openat` function with the "
"scheme-rooted path (`/scheme/{scheme-name}`) on the namespace file "
"descriptor to obtain the scheme's root file descriptor."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:34
msgid ""
"Kernel -> Namespace Manager: The Kernel forwards the request to the "
"Namespace Manager."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:35
msgid ""
"Namespace Manager -> Kernel: The Namespace Manager returns the scheme's root "
"file descriptor."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:36
msgid ""
"Kernel -> Application: The Kernel adds the scheme's root file descriptor "
"into the Application's file descriptor table."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:37
msgid ""
"Application -> Kernel: The application calls `openat` with `/path/to/file` "
"on the scheme's root file descriptor."
msgstr ""

#: src/communication.md:38
msgid "Kernel -> Scheme: The Kernel forwards the request to the target scheme."
msgstr ""

